eenville County","/arc-plc/south-carolina/greenville-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on Greenville County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. On the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids, September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025, November to December came in at 32% of normal on the middle of the grids, and in 2026 so far March to April sits at 41%. Grid 18189 had its driest year in 2016 at 64% of normal.</p>"}
